        "text": "NATIONAL ENERGY RETAIL RULES SCHEDULE 3\nVERSION 51 SAVINGS AND TRANSITIONAL RULES\nPage 212\n(2) Distributors must make the required alterations to their deemed connection\ncontracts by the effective date.\n(3) Alterations made under subrules (1) and (2) must take effect on and from the\neffective date.\n5 Medical confirmation form template\nThe AER must, by 1 March 2027, develop and publish the first medical\nconfirmation form template under new rule 123B.\n6 Distributor transitional obligations regarding life\nsupport registrations\n(1) A distributor must, on or promptly after the effective date, advise a retailer of the\nlife support requirements of any shared customer that immediately prior to the\neffective date is registered by the distributor under old rule 124(4) as having life\nsupport equipment ( distributor-registered customer ) including:\n(a) the life support equipment required by the life support user at the customer’s\npremises;\n(b) the date from which the life support equipment is required;\n(c) whether the customer has provided an old Part 7 medical confirmation and,\nif so, relevant information about that medical confirmation including the\ndate of that medical confirmation; and\n(d) whether the distributor has provided a deregistration notice to the customer\nprior to the effective date that has a date of deregistration after the effective\ndate.\n(2) Unless a distributor is notified by a retailer that it has deregistered a distributor-\nregistered customer under new rule 125 or the distributor has provided a notice to\nthe customer under new rule 126B(4), the distributor must comply with its\nobligations under new Part 7 in respect of a distributor-registered customer as if it\nhad been notified by the retailer of the distributor-registered customer's details\nunder new rule 124(1)(e).\n(3) If after the effective date but before 1 December 2029 the distributor receives an\nold Part 7 medical confirmation from a distributor-registered customer, the\ndistributor must advise the retailer that it has received the medical confirmation\nand provide the retailer with relevant information about that medical confirmation\nincluding the date of that medical confirmation.\n(4) The distributor must keep a copy of any old Part 7 medical confirmations\nprovided to it prior to 1 December 2029.\n(5) Subject to any applicable privacy laws, where a distributor-registered customer\nprovides an old Part 7 medical confirmation to the distributor before 1 December\n2029:\n(a) on request of the customer the distributor must provide a copy of the\nconfirmation to the customer within 15 business days of that request; and"
